        <mxCell id="r-safety" value="&lt;b&gt;Mandatory split prefix for every generated policy:&lt;/b&gt; tenant_id,…  &lt;b&gt;Why:&lt;/b&gt; tenant_id prevents cross-tenant Episodes. Rule-specific identity fields follow it. Native mode never publishes to Open-ITSI; open_itsi is the only external grouping path." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFF8F1;strokeColor=#C25700;strokeWidth=2;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=16;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=16;fontColor=#633000;" vertex="1" parent="r1"><mxGeometry x="220" y="1930" width="3760" height="150" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="r-default-note" value="&lt;b&gt;Default-policy caution:&lt;/b&gt; the stock ITSI Default Policy is not a C3 rule. Keep it outside the C3 result-policy allowlist; otherwise unmatched C3 Notables could create per-Notification Episodes and diverge from native behavior. The two former local-only policies—C3 Open-ITSI POC Grouping and Open ITSI Explicit Grouping—are intentionally absent." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F4F6F7;strokeColor=#7F8C8D;strokeWidth=2;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=16;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=15;fontColor=#34495E;" vertex="1" parent="r1"><mxGeometry x="220" y="2120" width="3760" height="140" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
